{"id": 32, "ts": 1780646647.3942635, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s focus on Candidate\u202fA\u2019s technical cognition, but as we\u2019ve seen, there is no concrete evidence of A\u2019s decision\u2011quality, attention to operational details, or day\u2011to\u2011day reliability. By contrast, Candidate\u202fC is explicitly described as \u201c100\u202f% reliable,\u201d \u201ccalm in a crisis,\u201d and able to \u201cmake correct decisions quickly.\u201d Those facts directly satisfy our core safety criteria of operational reliability, stress resilience, and decision quality. Moreover, C \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d indicating good crew cooperation despite the noted difficulty communicating ideas. While C\u2019s reluctance to pursue further education raises a modest adaptability concern, the lack of any evidence on B\u2019s decision quality, attention to detail, or proven reliability makes C a stronger overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role. Therefore, I shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**."}
